{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["And the reason for <b>whose stones are iron</b> — in a place where you would expect there to be stones, there you will find iron, for it is extracted from its dust. And it appears that in the land of Israel there is a quarry of copper and iron, which are a great necessity for the inhabitants of the land, and you shall lack nothing in it; but the finding of silver and gold is not a deficiency in the land. And in the Jerusalem Targum I saw: אבנהא ברירן היך פרזלא, etc., meaning that Scripture praises the land that quarries are found in it of great stones, precious stones, hewn stones, to build from them houses and walls and towers — not like the land of Egypt and many lands, whose inhabitants dwell in houses of clay, and those houses become their graves."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:46:50.912211596Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}